[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 1. Convert \(17_b\) to its base 10 equivalent:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 2. Convert \(97_b\) to its base 10 equivalent:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 3. For \(17_b\) to be a divisor of \(97_b\), \(9b + 7\) must be divisible by \(b + 7\). So, we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m for some integer \(k\). Rearrange this equation to solve for \(b\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m For \(b\) to be an integer, \(\frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k}\) must be an integer. This means \(9 - k\) must be a divisor of \(7(k - 1)\). Let's find the possible values of \(k\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m - If \(k = 8\), then \(b = \frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \frac{7 \cdot 7}{1} = 49\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m - If \(k = 7\), then \(b = \frac{7(7 - 1)}{9 - 7} = \frac{7 \cdot 6}{2} = 21\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=330779)[0m - If \(k = 10\), then \(b = \frac{7(10 - 1)}{9 - 10} = \frac{7 \cdot 9}{-1} = -63\) (not a valid base)
